<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dutugemunu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 161–137 BCE</span> · Also known as Dutthagamani, Duttha Gamani Abhaya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dutugemunu was a Sinhalese king of the Anuradhapura Kingdom who reigned from about 161 to 137 BCE. Son of King Kavantissa of Ruhuna in the south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, he defeated the Tamil ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ellalan">Elara</a> and united the island under one king. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahavamsa">Mahavamsa</a> chronicle celebrates him as a champion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a> and credits him with building the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruwanwelisaya">Ruwanwelisaya</a> stupa.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dutugemunu.jpg" alt="Dutugemunu" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Jolle~commonswiki assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anuradhapura17.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
